senses.gloss:
anikṣipta-dhura,
(1) adj. (= Pali anikkhittadhura), not laying down the burden, persevering: Bbh 〔203.21〕; Gv 〔514.18〕; ˚ra-tā, state of being persevering, AsP 〔287.15〕 etc.;
(2) n. of a Bodhisattva: Mvy 〔719〕; SP 〔3.5〕; Kv 〔1.11〕 (text ˚dhūra); Sukh 〔92.12〕.

aniyata, m.,
(1) with or sc. dharma (= Pali id., with dhamma), one of the two sorts of possible transgressions of monks which are undetermined as to type of offense and consequent punishment, i.e. of which the punishment depends on circumstances (Pali Vin. 〔iii.187—194〕; SBE 〔13.16 f.〕): dvāv aniyatau (sc. dharmau) Mvy 〔8382〕; dharmau Prāt 〔488.7〕;
(2) aniyata-gotra, or aniyataikatara-g˚, see s.v. gotra (1). See also s.v. rāśi.

a-nirvāha,
(1) m., no ‘exporting’, giving (of a girl) in marriage outside the clan: MSV 〔ii.7.4〕 (kanyāyā) ˚haḥ;
(2) Bhvr., not subject to this: ib. 〔ii.17.7〕 kanyā anirvāhā.

a-nilambha (as if from an unrecorded ni-lambh),
(1) adj., independent (Tib. on Mvy 〔619〕 brten pa med pa); as such, except in the next following cpds., only noted in Gv; sarvabhavānilambha-jñāna-gocarāḥ Gv 〔17.13〕; jñāne … anilambhe nirālaye 〔30.20〕; others 〔37.11〕, etc.;
(2) as subst., n. of a samādhi, ˚bha-samādhi-pratilabdho SP 〔424.3〕, for which Tib. strangely: rluṅ (wind, air) lha buḥi (= devaputrasya), (samādhi) of the wind-devaputra, or devaputra-wind, as if cpd. of anila! (with what?);
(3) n. of a kalpa: Gv 〔446.25〕. Cf. the following cpds.
